  "question": "Suppose that $a,b,c$ are three distinct real numbers. The expression $\\frac{(x-a)(x-b)}{(c-a)(c-b)}+\\frac{(x-b)(x-c)}{(a-b)(a-c)}+\\frac{(x-c)(x-a)}{(b-c)(b-a)}-1$ takes the value zero for",
  "options": {
    "A": "no real $x$",
    "B": "exactly two distinct real $x$",
    "C": "exactly three distinct real $x$",
    "D": "more than three real $x"
  },
  "answer": "D",
